@startuml
!include style.iuml
title Workspace persistence lifecycle
hide empty description
[*] --> Opening
Opening --> Saved : complete head\n+ writer lock
Opening --> ReadOnly : other tab\nowns writer lock
Opening --> Recovery : corrupt /\nunsupported storage
ReadOnly --> Opening : explicit takeover\nafter lock release
ReadOnly --> [*] : close
Saved --> Dirty : edit / accepted fix\n/ restore
Dirty --> Saving : autosave /\nexplicit save
Saving --> Saved : commit R\n[R is current]
Saving --> Dirty : commit R\n[newer edits exist]
Saving --> SaveFailed : quota / permission /\ntransaction error
SaveFailed --> Saving : explicit retry
SaveFailed --> Dirty : further edits / undo
SaveFailed --> [*] : close after loss\nwarning / export
Recovery --> Opening : select complete\ncheckpoint; retry
Recovery --> ReadOnly : inspect / export\nrecoverable content
Dirty --> [*] : explicit discard /\nexported recovery copy
Saved --> [*] : close
note right of Saving
OPFS verified before IDB head commit.
Failure never advances the head.
New edits stay dirty.
end note
note bottom of ReadOnly
Export status is separate.
It cannot mark local edits saved.
end note
@enduml
